WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.834 --> 00:00:03.033
-Welcome to the show.
It is very nice to meet you.

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:05.901
-It's nice meeting you as well.
-Did you see me?

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:07.000
Because we were at
the Met Gala last night.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.868
-I did. We made eye contact.

00:00:08.868 --> 00:00:09.968
-We kind of did
a little bit, right?

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:12.000
-And then we decided
not to say hi.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.200
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.801
We were standing in that line.

00:00:14.801 --> 00:00:16.234
-No.
-Yes.

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:17.667
-You were in the line?
-I was in the line.

00:00:17.667 --> 00:00:18.968
I saw you in front of me.

00:00:18.968 --> 00:00:21.067
And you looked back.
And then we made eye contact.

00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:22.767
And I go --
[ Inhales deeply ] No.

00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:26.234
-No. Save it.
Save the magic for Charades.

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:28.100
-Exactly.
-Yeah, and I think we did well.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:29.133
-We did.
-We did well.

00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:30.767
-We won.
-Yeah, we totally won.

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:31.834
Are you kidding me?
Of course.

00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:34.133
I want to know more about you.
-Okay.

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:35.901
-I know you live in L.A.

00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:37.934
Thank you for coming here to do
our show, but --

00:00:37.934 --> 00:00:40.067
-Thank you.
-You're from Spokane?

00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:42.300
-I am. Spokane, Washington.
-Washington.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.801
-My family loves that you
talk about Gonzaga.

00:00:44.801 --> 00:00:46.901
-Yeah! Yeah!
-Tell your family I said hi.

00:00:46.901 --> 00:00:47.901
-I will.
-Yeah, Gonzaga.

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:49.033
We were rooting for those kids.

00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:51.567
-Yeah, we were so excited.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:00:51.567 --> 00:00:57.300
And how do you go from Spokane
to here, to Hollywood?

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.501
-I was a little girl with
a big imagination.

00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:02.167
-Yeah, a dream.
Just a girl with a dream.

00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:03.200
-Yeah, my parents thought
it was like

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.367
wanting to be a princess.

00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:06.200
That it wasn't real,
you couldn't touch it.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:07.634
We're a smaller town.

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:11.000
So I put together a five-year
business plan presentation

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.200
of what could happen
if they let me.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.200
-Did you really?

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.300
-I did.
-I love this.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:16.868
-Yeah. They took me seriously.

00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:19.100
-A PowerPoint?
-A PowerPoint presentation.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.434
-For your parents.
-For my parents.

00:01:20.434 --> 00:01:21.601
-Like, "Hey,
if you let me do this,

00:01:21.601 --> 00:01:22.734
here's what I'll do.

00:01:22.734 --> 00:01:23.734
I'll make money here
and I'll live here."

00:01:23.734 --> 00:01:25.868
-I was, like, 11,
and they listened.

00:01:25.868 --> 00:01:28.701
-How did you have a plan?
How did you research it?

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:30.200
-I just googled a lot.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:32.133
-Yeah, on how to do it.

00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:33.334
-Google has
a lot of information.

00:01:33.334 --> 00:01:35.801
-Yeah. And did it take
five years or...?

00:01:35.801 --> 00:01:38.200
-It took a little longer.
-Yeah.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:39.367
-It took a little longer.

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:42.300
-Was it the struggle
you imagined? Or is it --

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:44.634
-It was a little harder
than I imagined.

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:46.067
-It's very -- It's tough.
-It is.

00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:47.234
It's tough to make it.

00:01:47.234 --> 00:01:48.701
-It's not as glamorous
as you think it is.

00:01:48.701 --> 00:01:52.033
-No, I mean, for some
people, you know, it is.

00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:53.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:54.467
-Okay. Okay.

00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:56.167
-It is a struggle, though.

00:01:56.167 --> 00:01:58.634
But it's a lot of work that
no one tells you really about.

00:01:58.634 --> 00:02:00.601
But you go from that PowerPoint

00:02:00.601 --> 00:02:02.701
to being on
the biggest show on TV.

00:02:02.701 --> 00:02:04.234
-Oh, gosh. Stop.
-"Euphoria."

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:06.067
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Congratulations.

00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:09.000
-Thank you.
-That's got to feel great.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.701
The first season was hit.

00:02:10.701 --> 00:02:11.901
And everyone's going,
"We love it."

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:14.501
Then second season,
I think, just took off.

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:16.167
Became a whole show of its own.

00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:17.634
-It did.
It became, like, it's own beast.

00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:19.901
-I know that it just exploded,
and everyone's talking about it.

00:02:19.901 --> 00:02:21.501
Everyone in our office
was talking about it,

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:24.367
and it became very big
as far as memes go.

00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:25.834
-It did.
-Yeah.

00:02:25.834 --> 00:02:27.934
You're very --
-It became very memable.

00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:29.667
-You're a very memable show.

00:02:29.667 --> 00:02:32.100
Of course, the "never ever
been happier" meme.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.200
-Yes.
-Look at you, though.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.968
-I have sent that to my mom.

00:02:36.968 --> 00:02:40.100
-You sent this --
-I sent that one to my mom.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.267 --> 00:02:42.300
-And did she laugh?
Did she love it?

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.334
-Yeah, she liked that one.

00:02:43.334 --> 00:02:45.934
-Yeah,
you've never been happier.

00:02:45.934 --> 00:02:47.567
Do you like doing
these dramatic scenes?

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:48.934
Like, how do you --
-I love them.

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:50.667
What's crazy,
though, is this scene

00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:54.400
was the first scene we filmed
coming back for season 2.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:57.200
So, we had an entire
year and a half break,

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:58.868
and then that was
the first scene we did.

00:02:58.868 --> 00:03:00.300
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:01.868
-And did you know it
was going to be --

00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:02.934
No idea.

00:03:02.934 --> 00:03:05.267
-They just put it in
different spots?

00:03:05.267 --> 00:03:07.334
-I didn't know how it would be.
-Yeah.

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:08.734
I forgot about this scene.
-Yeah.

00:03:08.734 --> 00:03:11.901
-We filmed for, like, almost
a year and then watched it.

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:12.968
-And then there it is.

00:03:12.968 --> 00:03:15.334
Well, there's another meme
here, too.

00:03:15.334 --> 00:03:17.601
This is Cassie,
your character Cassie.

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:20.834
And this is when you were in the
bathtub at the party, hiding.

00:03:20.834 --> 00:03:22.667
Oh, no.

00:03:22.667 --> 00:03:25.000
-"Me when the DoorDash person

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:27.033
knocks instead of just
leaving the food there."

00:03:27.033 --> 00:03:28.501
[ Laughter ]
"I'm not here!"

00:03:28.501 --> 00:03:30.133
I'm not --

00:03:30.133 --> 00:03:32.334
-But why is this so accurate?

00:03:32.334 --> 00:03:34.300
Why is this so accurate?

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:35.400
-It's almost like --

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:36.801
I'm like that
sometimes on Halloween.

00:03:36.801 --> 00:03:38.334
I'm like, "Alright, I gave
enough, trick or treaters.

00:03:38.334 --> 00:03:40.267
Let's go.
We're sleeping, we're sleeping."

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:41.634
-Why are we so scared of them?

00:03:41.634 --> 00:03:43.567
-I don't know. Just, come on.

00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:46.868
Just drop the food off.
We had a deal.

00:03:46.868 --> 00:03:48.334
This one, I love.

00:03:48.334 --> 00:03:51.934
This is "Cassie in high school
versus me in high school."

00:03:51.934 --> 00:03:53.734
-Oh, no.
-And everyone has done this.

00:03:53.734 --> 00:03:55.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.534 --> 00:03:59.868
Because just the way the
characters dress on "Euphoria."

00:03:59.868 --> 00:04:01.601
-They got their [bleep]
together.

00:04:01.601 --> 00:04:03.033
-Yeah, I mean, yes, they do.

00:04:03.033 --> 00:04:06.133
You can't say that on our show.
-Oh, I'm so sorry.

00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:07.934
-Yeah, no problem.
You can't say "together."

00:04:07.934 --> 00:04:09.934
You have to say --

00:04:09.934 --> 00:04:10.934
This just made me laugh,

00:04:10.934 --> 00:04:11.934
and then
everyone started doing it.

00:04:11.934 --> 00:04:13.300
And then, I told you that

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:14.467
we were going to
do this meme thing.

00:04:14.467 --> 00:04:16.267
And so you said,
"I'll help out," so...

00:04:16.267 --> 00:04:17.701
-Oh, no!

00:04:17.701 --> 00:04:19.200
-This is a picture of
you in high school.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:22.000
This is Cassie in high school
versus you in high school.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.100
Not --

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
There you go!

00:04:24.901 --> 00:04:27.167
-Oh, no!
-That's real!

00:04:27.167 --> 00:04:29.601
Come on, you're so cute.
Come on, buddy.

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:31.067
-Oh, man.

00:04:31.067 --> 00:04:33.501
The best part, too,
are my shoes.

00:04:33.501 --> 00:04:35.767
-What are you wearing?
-I'm wearing, like, Army boots.

00:04:35.767 --> 00:04:38.667
-Yes!
And how old are you there?

00:04:38.667 --> 00:04:40.667
-It's an old sweatshirt.

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:41.934
Because my family, we do

00:04:41.934 --> 00:04:43.300
Christmas sweatshirts
every year.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:44.501
So, it's old.

00:04:44.501 --> 00:04:46.734
But that was sophomore year.
-Sophomore year.

00:04:46.734 --> 00:04:47.834
Look at you now.

00:04:47.834 --> 00:04:49.601
I want to show everyone how

00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:51.234
incredible you are
in "Euphoria."

00:04:51.234 --> 00:04:53.100
You're really great.
Congratulations on that.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.400
Thank you.
-I'm a big fan.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:55.467
Please come back.

00:04:55.467 --> 00:04:57.234
Here's Sydney Sweeney
in "Euphoria."

00:04:57.234 --> 00:04:58.634
Take a look at this.

00:04:58.634 --> 00:05:00.167
-I deserve this, right?
-Oh, my God.

00:05:00.167 --> 00:05:01.868
Please, Mom, stop.

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:03.234
-I deserve this.
-Mom! Mom, stop!

00:05:03.234 --> 00:05:04.367
-You stop it.

00:05:04.367 --> 00:05:06.601
-Lexi, I'm going to ...
kill you.

00:05:06.601 --> 00:05:08.534
I deserve this, right?

00:05:08.534 --> 00:05:10.968
Because I've actually
lived a life.

00:05:10.968 --> 00:05:12.200
-Mom?

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:15.000
-I'm the one who takes risks.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.434
-Show us your boobs.

00:05:16.434 --> 00:05:19.234
-I'm the one who falls in love.

00:05:19.234 --> 00:05:23.734
-I'm the one who gets hurt,
not you, Lexi.

00:05:23.734 --> 00:05:25.367
[ Crowd murmurs ]

00:05:25.367 --> 00:05:29.167
You never even ... lived.

00:05:29.167 --> 00:05:34.000
That's why you're able to stand
up here and judge all of us!

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.467
You're just a ... bystander.

00:05:36.467 --> 00:05:39.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:39.634 --> 00:05:41.100
-Sydney Sweeney, everybody.

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:45.968
Seasons 1 and 2 of "Euphoria"
are streaming now on HBO Max.

